# Test Definition checksums (packet 06b) are sha256 of the file's bytes, so Git must never rewrite
# a schedule's line endings. core.autocrlf=true on Windows would turn LF into CRLF at checkout and
# every checksum in an .atedef would mismatch, refusing the run. Text stays LF for everyone.
*.tslua text eol=lf
*.lua text eol=lf
*.atedef text eol=lf
